       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. The maximum recommended amlodipine dose for adults is 10 mg once daily, and 50 mg is five times that. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Overdoses of that size can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change this.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail or older patient or one with hepatic impairment\n\nIf you do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you've confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
