       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I asked for a clinical reason and didn't get one. 50 mg of amlodipine daily is five times the maximum dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, the risk of severe hypotension and shock is real. Entering it as written could directly lead to patient harm.\n\nYou have some other options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Give me 5 mg or 10 mg once daily and I'll enter it now.\n- **Add more blood pressure control.** If 10 mg isn't enough, a second agent from a different class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, is the usual approach. I can enter that order if you tell me the drug and dose.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, they can review it with you. An order like this would normally need that review anyway.\n\nIf I've misunderstood something, for example if you meant a different drug or a different unit, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order."
      }
